From: Gcenx (macports-wine, emulators/wine-devel)
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Enable host Vulkan portability enumeration.

With the Khronos Vulkan loader on macOS, drivers such as MoltenVK are "portability" drivers and are only enumerated
when the instance asks for VK_KHR_portability_enumeration. This enables it when the host loader offers it.

Provenance (recorded by AnvilMac, 2026-10-15):
  Source:  https://github.com/Gcenx/macports-wine, commit 092031f7b987a1f1047f263ff3bfd4e1c9c850ee (2026-10-08),
           emulators/wine-devel/files/0001-win32u-Enable-host-Vulkan-portability-enumeration.diff
           (git blob 07cc6ea838276b6448ab16028957008ba8b83613), used by Gcenx's wine-devel 11.19 port.
  License: LGPL-2.1-or-later (Wine). Applied verbatim.
---
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
index 1bb4735587f..d8926c72198 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -449,6 +449,11 @@ static VkResult convert_instance_create_info( struct mempool *pool, VkInstanceCr
         instance->obj.extensions.has_VK_EXT_surface_maintenance1 = 1;
     if (vulkan_funcs.host_extensions.has_VK_KHR_get_physical_device_properties2)
         instance->obj.extensions.has_VK_KHR_get_physical_device_properties2 = 1;
+    if (vulkan_funcs.host_extensions.has_VK_KHR_portability_enumeration)
+    {
+        instance->obj.extensions.has_VK_KHR_portability_enumeration = 1;
+        info->flags |= VK_INSTANCE_CREATE_ENUMERATE_PORTABILITY_BIT_KHR;
+    }
     if (use_external_memory())
         instance->obj.extensions.has_VK_KHR_external_memory_capabilities = 1;
